        <headline>Hazardous Seas Warning issued September 25 at 1:48AM PDT until September 25 at 5:00AM PDT by NWS Medford OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Hazardous Seas Warning, very steep and hazardous
seas 9 to 11 ft at 9 seconds. For the Small Craft Advisory,
steep seas 7 to 9 ft at 9 seconds expected.

* WHERE...All of the area, but warning level seas, especially
north of Brookings early this morning, gradually becoming small
craft advisory all areas.

* WHEN...For the Hazardous Seas Warning, until 5 AM PDT early
this morning. For the Small Craft Advisory, from 5 AM early this
morning to 2 PM PDT this afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Very steep and hazardous seas could capsize or
damage vessels. Bar crossings will become especially
treacherous.

* View the hazard area in detail at https://go.usa.gov/x6hks
</description>
        <instruction>Recreational boaters should remain in port. Commercial vessels
should prepare for very steep seas and consider remaining in port
until conditions improve.</instruction>
